From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: give the boot-path prints a log level

A normal boot prints 67 lines from aic_load_fw and aic8800_fdrv at
KERN_WARNING although none reports a failure. 63 are bare printk() calls,
which use the default message level, and 4 are AICWFDBG(LOGERROR, ...)
for values that are not errors. "journalctl -p warning" therefore cannot
separate a failed radio from a working one.

Change the identity and proof lines (RELEASE DATE, chip_id, firmware path,
file md5, upload and patch version, aicwf_usb_disconnect) to pr_info(),
the progress lines to pr_debug(), and the four LOGERROR prints (Read FW
mem, p2p dev addr) to LOGINFO. No message text changes. The failure
prints keep their level.

Assisted-by: Claude

